  "state": {
    "case_id": "425",
    "case_summary": "A 68-year-old woman with Rai stage 0 chronic lymphocytic leukemia presented with a 2-day history of dyspnea on exertion. She reported no cough, chest pain, orthopnea, leg swelling, or viral-like symptoms.\n\nTemperature was 36.8°C, heart rate 102/min, respiratory rate 22/min, and blood pressure 124/76 mm Hg. She had conjunctival pallor and scleral icterus, but no lymphadenopathy, hepatosplenomegaly, or ecchymosis.\n\n- Laboratory Tests:     * Direct antiglobulin test (DAT) was positive for IgG    * DAT was negative for C3d    * Low haptoglobin    * High lactate dehydrogenase    * Reticulocytosis present        Note: The paper mentions a table of initial laboratory values, but the specific values are not provided in the text.",
